{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese","id":978139,"title":"Help me with Pookaese.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-28T19:25:29-07:00","id":978139,"title":"Help me with Pookaese.","content":"Its a bit of an art, that on the surface looks simple, but when your trying to &quot;Communicate the truth&quot;<br /> <br /> ideas on how to do so relatively artfully","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:59:32-07:00","id":978155,"title":"","content":"I once played a Pooka who primarily communicated in idiom. Inspired by the &quot;Darmok&quot; episode of TNG. <br /> <br /> It was a big hit, but it required a lot of preparation and got exhausting by the end of a session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:37:59-07:00","id":978192,"title":"","content":"I interpret it to mean that pooka can speak in riddles, metaphors or slang. Pig Latin is a good option, for instance. I actually find saying the opposite of what you mean or lying all the time is the hardest to maintain and the hardest to decipher. It's also the least interesting way to run a pooka.<br /> <br /> The old kithbook had some ideas that were decent. Personally, I find the kith flaw virtually unplayable as written. But making your character speak in poetry or rap lyrics, for instance, can be way more fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T23:34:58-07:00","id":978242,"title":"","content":"I really hope they fixed that one. Never being able to enter a password without a Willpower point is going to suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T02:01:07-07:00","id":978272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=978242#post978242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope they fixed that one. Never being able to enter a password without a Willpower point is going to suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha! Indeed!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T05:35:48-07:00","id":978326,"title":"","content":"Answer questions with questions, exaggerate, throw in random details that never happened.<br /> <br /> Pooka: &quot;And then the Count walked in. He looked magnificent in his red over coat!&quot;<br /> <br /> Eshu: &quot;But wasn't it a blue over coat?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pooka: &quot;Nope, that blue tint was just a trick of the light off those shiny buttons!&quot;<br /> <br /> Eshu: &quot;Are you sure?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pooka: &quot;If perception is subjective, who can really be sure of anything?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pooka are so much fun to play! Hopefully folks will find them a bit more accessible in C20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:35:03-07:00","id":978387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=978326#post978326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Answer questions with questions, exaggerate, throw in random details that never happened.<br /> <br /> Pooka: &quot;And then the Count walked in. He looked magnificent in his red over coat!&quot;<br /> <br /> Eshu: &quot;But wasn't it a blue over coat?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pooka: &quot;Nope, that blue tint was just a trick of the light off those shiny buttons!&quot;<br /> <br /> Eshu: &quot;Are you sure?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pooka: &quot;If perception is subjective, who can really be sure of anything?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pooka are so much fun to play! Hopefully folks will find them a bit more accessible in C20.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, ask questions and give people and things nicknames.<br /> <br /> Ferret Pooka: &quot;The Ducks are about again&quot;<br /> Monkey Pooka: &quot;Again? Did you look at the mess they made last time?&quot;<br /> Ferret Pooka: &quot;Let's be honest here: it was the wolves that started the mess.&quot;<br /> Monkey Pooka: &quot;Wolves come around causing trouble. The Ducks get involved and things get messier.&quot;<br /> Ferret Pooka: &quot;At least the ducks clean up the mess afterwards.&quot;<br /> Monkey Pooka: &quot;Do you think the Ducks can clean up the entire mess this time?&quot;<br /> Ferret Pooka: *thinks* &quot;We should help the ducks clean up the mess.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> No one figured out (besides our Slaugh childer motley mate) who the ducks were.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Duck - House Gwydion (Because Sidhe &quot;quack&quot; alot)<br /> Wolves - Shadow Court<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-29-2016, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:18:54-07:00","id":978492,"title":"","content":"oh in a game Was just playing in, a Pooka NPC was talking with a Sidhe visitor saying &quot;Our Seelie Masters have been very Generous. I have totally forgiven them for killing my mentor on the night of iron knives, water under the bridge and all that. The Seelie are Widely hated in this town, but theirs quite an undercurrent of people who think their really nice guys, but not enough to help them any.&quot;<br /> <br /> How could that have been put in riddles or pig latin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:27:37-07:00","id":978577,"title":"","content":"Sarcasm is a great tool as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you know what was easy? Forgiving the Seelie for the Night of Iron Knives. I didn't lose anything important that night- just my mentor. But do you know agree that time moves on and heals all wounds?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Most people in this town just LOVE the Seelie. They love them so much, they would hang their corpses off the oak in town square. Yet if you listen carefully to the whispers on the wind, you'll know the truth. If Seelie corpses hang off the oak tree, the whispers will try to paint the town red. But what use is whispers on the wind to the Seelie?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pooka talk is easier when you have someone to bounce off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:28:52-07:00","id":978672,"title":"","content":"ok still trying to develop my talent for it<br /> <br /> And in the thing in question the Seelie were, for the most part tolerated, even liked, though their was an undercurrent of resentment.<br /> <br /> is saying &quot;I feel young and spry for my age&quot; the best way to say &quot;I feel old and world weary for my age&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:04:57-07:00","id":978725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=978672#post978672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok still trying to develop my talent for it<br /> <br /> And in the thing in question the Seelie were, for the most part tolerated, even liked, though their was an undercurrent of resentment.<br /> <br /> is saying &quot;I feel young and spry for my age&quot; the best way to say &quot;I feel old and world weary for my age&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use metaphors, which are technically lies. &quot;My bones are old as the hills. My soul worn down as the mountains.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Pooka's words are rarely going to be translated word for word. But you can convey the general meaning behind it.<br /> <br /> A Pooka may try to convey &quot;I hate that Unseelie bastard because he killed my daughter and I want him to die.&quot; The listener may understand the Pooka wants the Unseelie bastard to die because he did something bad to him. An astute listener may realize the Unseelie bastard took someone close to the Pooka. Someone who knows the Pooka's story will realize exact what the Pooka is trying to say.<br /> <br /> Either way the listener is going to go kill the Pooka's enemy, which is what he wanted in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-29-2016, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:03:31-07:00","id":978743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=978326#post978326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Answer questions with questions, exaggerate, throw in random details that never happened.<br /> <br /> Pooka: &amp;quot;And then the Count walked in. He looked magnificent in his red over coat!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Eshu: &amp;quot;But wasn't it a blue over coat?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Pooka: &amp;quot;Nope, that blue tint was just a trick of the light off those shiny buttons!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Eshu: &amp;quot;Are you sure?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Pooka: &amp;quot;If perception is subjective, who can really be sure of anything?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Pooka are so much fun to play! Hopefully folks will find them a bit more accessible in C20.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are great fun. But the flaw was written before email, ATMs, and cell phones were wide spread. Now a Pooka is nearly impossible to play without a constant stream of Willpower points. Need to use your debit card, enter your pin. Willpower point. Checking your email, need a password. Willpower point. Need to unlock your phone. Willpower point. It's just bad design unless this was fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:41:54-07:00","id":978768,"title":"","content":"So be flexible with it? The spirit of the flaw is that pooka cause chaos and lie to people in their communications. They're not communicating with a computer, so there's no one to lie to.<br /> <br /> Flaws add spice and make things interesting. They're not meant to be debilitating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:42:22-07:00","id":978769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=978743#post978743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are great fun. But the flaw was written before email, ATMs, and cell phones were wide spread. Now a Pooka is nearly impossible to play without a constant stream of Willpower points. Need to use your debit card, enter your pin. Willpower point. Checking your email, need a password. Willpower point. Need to unlock your phone. Willpower point. It's just bad design unless this was fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a pooka should loose willpower for giving thier password to a computer program. Though I expect some interesting answers for thier security questions. <br /> <br /> Now if someone (a person) asks for thier password, I except lies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:41:04-07:00","id":979113,"title":"","content":"You could just apply the flaw whenever a pooka is asked a direct question. That makes sense, and probably makes the flaw less debilitating. Or you could allow a Willpower roll instead of a Willpower point for the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T21:10:42-07:00","id":980568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=978768#post978768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So be flexible with it? The spirit of the flaw is that pooka cause chaos and lie to people in their communications. They're not communicating with a computer, so there's no one to lie to.<br /> <br /> Flaws add spice and make things interesting. They're not meant to be debilitating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then don't write them in a debilitating way. These are the rules of an RPG. Some people will be flexible with them, others will be utter dicks. So instead of crossing our fingers and hoping the Storyteller will be generous, how about writing the flaw well in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:12:39-07:00","id":980596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=980568#post980568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then don't write them in a debilitating way. These are the rules of an RPG. Some people will be flexible with them, others will be utter dicks. So instead of crossing our fingers and hoping the Storyteller will be generous, how about writing the flaw well in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I find the flaw makes the pooka unplayable as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T07:18:23-07:00","id":980761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=980568#post980568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then don't write them in a debilitating way.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were written a couple of years before I discovered Changeling: The Dreaming. I also didn't write them in C20. That being being said, pooka are one of my all time favorite things in the game. If their flaw was to drastically change, that's something that would make the game unrecognizable for me. Obviously, some people find pooka unplayable, but other folks <b>love</b> playing pooka.<br /> <br /> That's the nice thing about pen and paper role playing games though \u2014 they're not computer games. If something in it doesn't suit you or isn't fun for a group as written, there's nothing to stop you from changing things up to make the game more enjoyable for you. It's nothing bad. It's not breaking rules. It's just seasoning the game to taste.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:23:27-07:00","id":980813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=980761#post980761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were written a couple of years before I discovered Changeling: The Dreaming. I also didn't write them in C20. That being being said, pooka are one of my all time favorite things in the game. If their flaw was to drastically change, that's something that would make the game unrecognizable for me. Obviously, some people find pooka unplayable, but other folks <b>love</b> playing pooka.<br /> <br /> That's the nice thing about pen and paper role playing games though \u2014 they're not computer games. If something in it doesn't suit you or isn't fun for a group as written, there's nothing to stop you from changing things up to make the game more enjoyable for you. It's nothing bad. It's not breaking rules. It's just seasoning the game to taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are my favorite kith as well, which is why I care. Please know that I'm not blaming you personally, you just happen to be the closest thing to a OP / WW person who's taken an interest in regularly posting here. And at present you're defending poorly written rules. Sure, changing what's written isn't breaking the rules, it's making house rules to fix obvious developer mistakes in order to make a WW / OP game playable. Something that shouldn't have to be done, but frequently does need doing.<br /> <br /> Just like we can acknowledge years later that 1s cancelling successes is simply bad rules, we can also acknowledge that the pooka flaw in the modern context is simply unplayable. There's no shame in admitting there's a problem and fixing it, but there is shame in refusing to acknowledge there's even a problem. <br /> <br /> I mean, seriously. The entire cantrip system is being overhauled because it's borked. But an entire kith being unplayable as written is left to fester.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11658,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","user":"Rabbit Pooka","date":". 10-03-2016, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:44:07-07:00","id":980831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=978326#post978326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully folks will find them a bit more accessible in C20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you missed this bit of what I said earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:59:20-07:00","id":980843,"title":"","content":"well its good to know that kind of issues getting looked at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:09:35-07:00","id":980854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=980831#post980831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you missed this bit of what I said earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the flaw's rewritten or it's made explicitly clear that passwords, PIN numbers (yes, I know it's redundant), account numbers, name when speaking to police / TSA agents, and a thousand other situations are not included in the flaw, then you missed the bit where pooka are unplayable as written. As written they're the lawful stupid and fishmalks of Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:39:54-07:00","id":980881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=980854#post980854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then you missed the bit where pooka are unplayable as written. As written they're the lawful stupid and fishmalks of Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably where I should bow out of this conversation. I doubt I'll have anything constructive to add that I haven't already said.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:53:26-07:00","id":980885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=980854#post980854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the flaw's rewritten or it's made explicitly clear that passwords, PIN numbers (yes, I know it's redundant), account numbers, name when speaking to police / TSA agents, and a thousand other situations are not included in the flaw, then you missed the bit where pooka are unplayable as written. As written they're the lawful stupid and fishmalks of Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As someone who played Pooka for over a year, I don't find the flaw makes the splat any more unplayable than say a Childer. &quot;Flaw only comes into affect when talking to a person. Computer programs and the like don't count.&quot; isn't that bad of a house rule. It would be nice for that rule to be included into the new edition.<br /> <br /> For TSA agents, Police, and the like, the Pooka can spend willpower or have another PC help them out &quot;Oh, don't mind Oot. She's drunk. I'm her Designated Driver. What can I help you with, officer?&quot; Besides the occasional tense session, I doubt a Pooka is going to spend that many games being questioned by the police.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-03-2016, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:13:42-07:00","id":981013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=980885#post980885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As someone who played Pooka for over a year, I don't find the flaw makes the splat any more unplayable than say a Childer. &quot;Flaw only comes into affect when talking to a person. Computer programs and the like don't count.&quot; isn't that bad of a house rule. It would be nice for that rule to be included into the new edition.<br /> <br /> For TSA agents, Police, and the like, the Pooka can spend willpower or have another PC help them out &quot;Oh, don't mind Oot. She's drunk. I'm her Designated Driver. What can I help you with, officer?&quot; Besides the occasional tense session, I doubt a Pooka is going to spend that many games being questioned by the police.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've never found a PC telling the true to Police officers to ever come up...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:49:25-07:00","id":981038,"title":"","content":"On a slightly different note, how do people feel about giving some benefits to Banality (at a high cost) like Shadow Dice, Rage or Demon Arts? Something more concrete than the often abused and never very clear 'rule of nope' (gain a point of Banality and ignore a cantrip). It would give Grumps something of a benefit over Childlings. For instance, if Banality can be substituted for Glamour to resist magic. Instead of unweaving and releasing magic, or reshaping it, Banality would just crush it. It would be slightly easier (difficulty 5) but every success garners an extra point of Banality. Maybe Banality can be used to hide your fae nature from Auspex or Kenning by denying your mien temporarily. Agendas never really made much sense to me, but something that makes Banality useful (even if painful) would help stress that duality between fae and mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:01:37-07:00","id":981047,"title":"","content":"This might ought to be it's own topic, but check it out! Something akin to that already exists \u2014 Changeling: The Dreaming 2nd Edition, page 206: Invoking Banality<br /> <br /> If it can be used to deny cantrips, I don't see why it couldn't be used to deny other Glamorous things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:05:41-07:00","id":981050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=981038#post981038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a slightly different note, how do people feel about giving some benefits to Banality (at a high cost) like Shadow Dice, Rage or Demon Arts? Something more concrete than the often abused and never very clear 'rule of nope' (gain a point of Banality and ignore a cantrip). It would give Grumps something of a benefit over Childlings. For instance, if Banality can be substituted for Glamour to resist magic. Instead of unweaving and releasing magic, or reshaping it, Banality would just crush it. It would be slightly easier (difficulty 5) but every success garners an extra point of Banality. Maybe Banality can be used to hide your fae nature from Auspex or Kenning by denying your mien temporarily. Agendas never really made much sense to me, but something that makes Banality useful (even if painful) would help stress that duality between fae and mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always thought banality should be sort of seductive, like shadow dice. Every action bringing you closer and each time rationalizing a little bit more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:32:45-07:00","id":981073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=981047#post981047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might ought to be it's own topic, but check it out! Something akin to that already exists \u2014 Changeling: The Dreaming 2nd Edition, page 206: Invoking Banality<br /> <br /> If it can be used to deny cantrips, I don't see why it couldn't be used to deny other Glamorous things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought I'd read it but could never find the text, so I assumed it was a house rule! My bad.<br /> <br /> The other mentions of invoking Banality seem to imply characters just go 'nope', gain a point of Banality, and ignore the Glamour. I think one of the examples was if a human sees a flying nocker and nopes them out of the sky (possibly shunting them into the Dreaming). I guess it's just another of those things that wasn't always 100% clear, or it could be my foggy memory over the years...<br /> <br /> Though you're right, this probably does need another thread. I'd like to see some Banality subsystems that can replace Agendas and give Grumps something of a foot up. I'll start a new thread in the morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:55:48-07:00","id":981182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/978139-help-me-with-pookaese?p=981013#post981013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've never found a PC telling the true to Police officers to ever come up...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Good point!<br /> <br /> <br /> Any who, a thought occurred to me. A Pooka that is obviously lying, being sarcastic, and using metaphors is not a Pooka you need to worry about. It's the honest sounding Pooka you should watch out for. <br /> <br /> Much like sane seeming Malkavians. <br /> <br /> Also, if a Pooka is a Used Car Salesman, what should his animal form be? A rat? A lizard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T21:32:41-07:00","id":981260,"title":"","content":"Would the &quot;banal&quot; account of what's going on be considered the truth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T01:10:31-07:00","id":981332,"title":"","content":"I find the way that Pooka flaw is written in the preview for C20 way easier to manage than the flaw in 2nd Edition. Deception is only required when asked a direct question. Also the spirit of the Pooka flaw is verbal communication, not writing or typing. When a computer prompts for a password or an atm for a PIN number, its a machine requesting an action not a person asking for information. The pooka flaw is meant to impact one's communication with sentient beings capable of discourse, not automated programs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}